# MissDCv2

Assume:

```text
MISSDCV2/missdcv2.jar

data/<dataset>/<mechanism>/<ratio>/<repetition>/dirty.csv
```

## Run with the default configuration

```bash
java -jar MISSDCV2/missdcv2.jar \
  data/<dataset>/<mechanism>/<ratio>/<repetition>/dirty.csv
```

This runs MissDCv2 with the **default final configuration**:

```text
DC discovery              = exact
minimum evidence count    = 8
maximum DC size            = 7
voting                     = tuple
ML                         = disabled
fallback                   = disabled
```

Example:

```bash
java -jar MISSDCV2/missdcv2.jar \
  data/adult/MCAR/0.05/1/dirty.csv
```

The output is written beside the input:

```text
data/adult/MCAR/0.05/1/dirty_imputed.csv
```

## Override parameters

You only need to provide options when testing a configuration different from the defaults.

For example, use evidence multiplicity 4:

```bash
java -jar MISSDCV2/missdcv2.jar \
  data/adult/MCAR/0.05/1/dirty.csv \
  --min-evidence-multiplicity 4
```

Use maximum DC size 5:

```bash
java -jar MISSDCV2/missdcv2.jar \
  data/adult/MCAR/0.05/1/dirty.csv \
  --dc-size-max 5
```

Change both:

```bash
java -jar MISSDCV2/missdcv2.jar \
  data/adult/MCAR/0.1/1/dirty.csv \
  --min-evidence-multiplicity 4 \
  --dc-size-max 5
```

Enable ML completion:

```bash
java -jar MISSDCV2/missdcv2.jar \
  data/adult/MCAR/0.1/1/dirty.csv \
  --mode dc-ml
```

Change voting:

```bash
java -jar MISSDCV2/missdcv2.jar \
  data/adult/MCAR/0.1/1/dirty.csv \
  --voting current
```

Available voting modes are:

```text
current
tuple
dc
```

## Disk cleanup

After scoring the result, remove:

```text
data/<dataset>/<mechanism>/<ratio>/<repetition>/dirty_imputed.csv
```

The comparison script should therefore:

```text
run JAR → score dirty_imputed.csv → record results → delete dirty_imputed.csv
```
